WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.270
Occasionally, Fox News host Chris Wallace
will bring us some kind of like heroic journalism

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.900
by American standards, but it's really what
in other countries would just be called journalism.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.759
And today's is perfect because it shows us
how easily a talking point that spreads like

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:19.510
wildfire can be exposed and debunked.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.980
If reporters are actually willing to do it
in many, many are not, or at least they're

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.561
not well-prepared enough to do it.

00:00:25.561 --> 00:00:31.789
And the talking point in this case is that
stimulus checks are going to prisoners.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:37.170
Republicans have, among other things, been
saying Democrats and Joe Biden are sending

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:44.429
stimulus checks to people in prison and some
senators say it and then right wing media

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:45.429
says it.

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:50.230
And then before you know it, it's being repeated
by Republican voters in diners, the likes

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.499
of which we saw in clips earlier today.

00:00:53.499 --> 00:00:59.280
The truth, of course, is that prisoners got
stimulus money during the first covid stimulus

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.339
package and during the second covid stimulus
package.

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:04.140
It's how they work.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:10.100
It's not set up to exclude people who are
otherwise income eligible just because they're

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.490
in prison now.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:16.050
Maybe it could be done logistically, but a
court has actually said, no, you can't do

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.070
it.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:23.890
And so radical Republican Senator Tom Cotton
pulls this bullet point and Chris Wallace

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.890
confronts him.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:30.350
Check out Tom Cotton's defense and Chris Wallace
confronting Tom Cotton with his own previous

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.350
words here.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:36.100
Here is one of your other complaints about
the covid relief bill.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.370
Take a look, sir.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:43.200
How crazy some of the Democratic ideas are,
I mean, they had a chance on Saturday morning

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.130
to stop checks from going to prisoners, from
going to the Boston bomber, for instance.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.950
And on that vote, they declined.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:56.600
Every single Democrat wanted to continue the
practice of sending checks to prisoners.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.710
But Senator, under two previous covid related
bills that you supported and voted for and

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:08.060
the president runs on prisoners also got checks
in those bills.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.720
Well, Chris, that was obviously never Congress's
intent.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.920
The Trump administration, IRS and Treasury
Department did not send checks to prisoners.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.760
Liberal advocacy groups sued to try to force
that a liberal judge that they had to last

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:22.760
month was that far.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.010
This month was the first time we ever had
a simple up or down vote on whether those

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.640
checks should go to prisoners.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.610
And the simple fact is that every Democrat
voted to keep sending checks to prisoners.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.120
I don't think that's a smart idea.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.300
I suspect most Americans don't either.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.160
So notice how Tom Cotton tries like a mini
Gish Gallop there.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.330
Gish Gallop is where you throw a bunch of
stuff out and it's sort of all together.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.370
Sounds like, wow, that's a lot.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:48.370
But then when you start going through each
claim, you realize there's nothing there.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.630
First, Tom Cotton concedes.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.410
OK, yes.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.820
Stimulus checks went to prisoners during Trump's
covid stimulus.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:01.110
No one checks went to prisoners during Trump's
covid stimulus number two.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.130
And now checks are going to prisoners during
the third stimulus under Joe Biden.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:11.030
But says Tom Cotton, during the first and
second ones, it wasn't our intent.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:15.970
We didn't want them to go to prisoners this
time.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.530
Democrats do want the checks to go to prisoners.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:23.700
It was never their intention, he says, but
they did it twice and then they only are making

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:28.140
a big deal out of it the third time when Joe
Biden is president and Democrats control the

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.140
Senate.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:34.660
But then Tom Cotton says this is the first
time we actually had an up or down vote on

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.430
it and it passed.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:41.230
Well, that's because you guys controlled the
Senate before and you didn't want an up and

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.230
down vote.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:46.440
But more importantly, the up and down vote
this time was irrelevant because it's already

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:52.540
been decided on previously by a federal judge,
the IRS inspector general, previously after,

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.400
I believe it was after the second stimulus
bill, might have been the first.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:02.010
I think it was the second the IRS inspector
general confirmed that they did send checks

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.209
to prisoners during one of the earlier stimulus
packages.

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:10.800
And because there were no restrictions on
people in jail or prison getting the money,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.790
the IRS later was pressured to change their
position.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.859
And the IRS said, you know what, prisoners
don't qualify for the release checks.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.400
And if anybody got one, they should send the
money back.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.860
So prisoners filed a class action lawsuit
against the IRS.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:30.560
And the treasury secretary and a federal judge
ruled on this in September.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:37.370
The court ruling said you can't withhold coronavirus
relief payments if prisoners qualify from

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.680
an income standpoint just because they are
incarcerated, a federal judge decided.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.530
So this up and down vote now was meaningless
in the end.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:52.290
And recall that prisoners have to buy their
own hygiene products.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.480
They pay exorbitant rates just to make phone
calls.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.740
That's another big scam that preys on prisoners,
which we've talked about.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.270
Give them the stimulus money, guys.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:05.730
We're talking about stimulus money that went
to hundreds of millions of people.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:09.630
There's a couple million prisoners that that
this applied to.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.160
Let's not stand in the way.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:17.650
But more importantly, Tom Cotton is such a
hypocrite and his defense is so, you know,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.740
I want to say it's so obviously bogus.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.440
If it weren't for Chris Wallace saying, whoa,
whoa, whoa, stop the clock here, a lot of

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.260
people probably would fall for Tom Cotton's
explanation.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.270
And in fact, many people do because they see
Chris Wallace and they're like, that's like

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.270
when Shep Smith was on Fox.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.690
He's the one guy you can't trust on Fox News.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:42.340
That's unfortunately the perspective of of
many of these right wing Fox viewers.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:49.160
But the talking point falls apart so quickly
and yet it still spreads like wildfire.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.360
So nice job, mostly by Chris Wallace.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:55.220
This is just kind of called journalism in
many other countries, but I would have like

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:55.800
to see him push back even more.

